{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "purpose": "THE canonical AST contract, machine-readable and normative. Six projection surfaces declare this same shape again in their own language -- a Swift struct cannot be produced by a C function and neither can a Kotlin class or a TypeScript interface -- and scripts/audit-ast-projections.mjs checks every one of them against this file. The prose companion at docs/specs/canonical-ast.md carries everything a table cannot say (the core rules, coordinates, ownership, the attribute grammar) and ITS table is generated from this file and checked against it, so the two cannot drift. Until Step 15A both lived under docs/deprecated/, which docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md says is archive and not normative, while four executable policy files read them.",
